{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet7SA7BEvG5qeCewUWmQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The existing tests pass. Now I have a clear picture of the codebase. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add a new ErrorCode enum value `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to represent when a shipment cannot be confirmed due to its status (e.g., when it's CANCELLED). This follows the existing convention of semantic error codes like `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Finds the shipment by ID (throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND if not found)\n   - If shipment status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves it\n   - If shipment status is already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent behavior)\n   - If shipment status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - Returns the shipment in the response\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four new test cases:\n   - Test that confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED status\n   - Test that confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change (idempotency)\n   - Test that confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with appropriate error code\n   - Test that confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n\nI considered creating a service layer (ShipmentService) to handle the confirm logic, but the existing codebase has no service layer—all logic is directly in the controller. Adding a service layer would violate the requirement to \"preserve the existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture.\"\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):**\n   - Client: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Controller: Load shipment, check status\n   - Controller: If CREATED, update status to CONFIRMED\n   - Repository: `save()` the updated shipment\n   - Response: 200 OK with updated Shipment JSON\n\n2. **Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED):**\n   - Client: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Controller: Load shipment, check status\n   - Controller: If CONFIRMED, return as-is without saving\n   - Response: 200 OK with unchanged Shipment JSON\n\n3. **Conflict path (CANCELLED):**\n   - Client: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Controller: Load shipment, check status\n   - Controller: If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM, message)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler: Convert to 409 ApiError response\n   - Response: 409 Conflict with ApiError envelope\n\n4. **Not found path:**\n   - Client: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Controller: Load shipment returns null\n   - Controller: Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler: Convert to 404 ApiError response\n   - Response: 404 Not Found with ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1**: Confirm a shipment in CREATED status → verify status changes to CONFIRMED and persists\n- **Test 2**: Create a shipment, confirm it, then confirm again → verify second confirm succeeds and status is still CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n- **Test 3**: Create a CANCELLED shipment (directly in repository), attempt to confirm → verify 409 response with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM error code\n- **Test 4**: Attempt to confirm a non-existent shipment → verify 404 response with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":21892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":189},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f783d76-7c83-4342-a17e-342901b1cbb6","uuid":"06fcfa52-44f0-483b-b16e-6ac927887c41","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:35:48.108Z","request_id":"req_011Cet7S9DrDAQyhTscpV8Go"}
